infographic compare-binary-horizontal-underline-text-vs
data
  title Version selection: Go MVS vs npm semver ranges
  desc Why the same go.mod reproduces forever while the same package.json needs a lockfile
  compares
    - label Go MVS — deterministic by construction
      children
        - label require = minimum, not a range
          desc A require line is a floor; the graph never floats above what was asked for
        - label Max of the minimums wins
          desc Smallest version satisfying every module — never the latest release
        - label No lockfile for version selection
          desc The build list is a pure function of go.mod — any machine, any day, identical
        - label Upgrades only when you ask
          desc go get raises a minimum; no auto bugfix pickup, offset by govulncheck
    - label npm semver ranges — resolved at install time
      children
        - label ^1.3.0 is a range
          desc package.json declares a band, not a fixed version
        - label Latest compatible wins
          desc The same manifest yields different trees on different days
        - label Lockfile bolted on
          desc package-lock.json restores the determinism the model lacks
        - label Automatic bugfix pickup
          desc Fresh patches by default, at the cost of reproducibility
theme
  palette #14b8a6 #f43f5e
